/ActualText (Grading handwritten exams is time-consuming, inconsistent, and prone to fatigue-induced bias. To solve this, develop a Human-in-the-Loop \(HITL\) grading pipeline that uses Vision-Language Models \(VLMs\) and Agentic LLMs to evaluate scanned exams against strict rubrics.\nThe system will allow professors to upload bulk exam scans and JSON rubrics. It will automatically extract, transcribe, and grade complex handwritten answers, awarding partial credit with justifications. These AI-proposed grades are then pushed to a high-speed dashboard, allowing Teaching Assistants \(TAs\) to rapidly review, approve, or override the decisions, ensuring fairness and massive time savings.\()
